  "content_description": "Action Item - Teams",
  "content_text_body": "Managers and team leaders, along with team members, have a responsibility to help ensure an effective decision-making process is in place.  \n\n### Reflect on the team leader's decision-making process\n\nSpend 15 minutes this week individually thinking about your leader's and your own strengths and weaknesses when it comes to decision making. Answer these questions:\n\n* Do I/they speed up decision making or slow it down?\n\n* Do I/they facilitate decision making or impede it?\n\n* Do I/they make unilateral decisions or seek multiple points of view?\n\nIdentify which, if any, changes are needed for the team to make better decisions. \n\n### Identify growth opportunities \n\nIn a team meeting or 1 on 1s, discuss: 1) the strengths of the leader in this regard and how these help your team succeed and 2) at least one specific way the manager/team leader could improve to help the team be even more successful.",
